# Intentionally empty. Passed as `wrangler dev --env-file` by
# tools/verify-edge-connectivity.mjs.
#
# Without it, wrangler loads the repo-root `.env` and re-injects
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN into the dev session, which then fails with
#
#   ✘ [ERROR] This Worker uses bindings that need to run remotely, even when
#   developing locally, but the remote session could not be authenticated.
#   It looks like you are authenticating via a custom API token
#   (CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN) set in an environment variable.
#
# An API token cannot open a remote-binding session at all — the edge-preview
# endpoint answers `10405 Method not allowed for this authentication scheme` —
# so the token has to be out of the way for the `wrangler login` OAuth session
# to be used. Blanking the variable in the environment is NOT sufficient here,
# because wrangler reads the root `.env` itself.
#
# ADR 006 records the blanking rule for the build; this file is the equivalent
# for `wrangler dev`. Do not delete it because it "looks empty".
